{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"why-kirana","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why Kirana"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"CSS-in-JS\" means two different things, and most of the dislike is for the\nfirst one. This page separates them, says what Kirana is, what it answers that\nStyleX left open, and where it costs you something."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-css-in-js-people-left","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The CSS-in-JS people left"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first generation (styled-components, Emotion and their relatives) kept\nstyles in JavaScript and turned them into CSS "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"in the browser, while\nrendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Every component that rendered serialised its styles, hashed them\nand inserted a "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">style</span>&gt;","source":"<style>"}},{"type":"text","value":" rule. That had costs that no amount of tuning removed:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work on every render."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Styles were computed at runtime, so pages started\nslower and got slower as the number of components grew."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A library in every bundle."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The runtime that did that work shipped to every\nuser."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server rendering got harder."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Styles had to be collected during the render\nand serialised into the HTML."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser recalculated styles more often."}]},{"type":"text","value":" React's own documentation\nlists two problems with runtime "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">style</span>&gt;","source":"<style>"}},{"type":"text","value":" injection: it \"forces the browser to\nrecalculate the styles a lot more often\", and it \"can be very slow if it\nhappens at the wrong time in the React lifecycle\". It recommends\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useInsertionEffect","children":[{"type":"text","value":"static extraction to CSS files, plus inline styles for dynamic values"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\nand says the first of those two problems \"is not solvable\" for runtime\ninjection."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub's Primer is the public example. Starting with Primer React v37 it moved\nits components from styled-components to CSS Modules, finished that by December\n2024, and reports "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"55 % less time to server-render a page and 25 % less time for\nthe components on a page to initialise"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n("},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.blog/engineering/architecture-optimization/improving-site-performance-by-shipping-more-css/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub Engineering, 2026"}]},{"type":"text","value":").\nIts stated reasons were exactly the list above: styles initialised on the client,\nserver rendering slowed by style collection, and style updates that \"grew out of\ncontrol as component count grew\"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is a verdict on "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runtime"}]},{"type":"text","value":" CSS-in-JS. It is not a verdict on writing styles\nnext to components."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-compiler-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a compiler changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A compiled system reads the same style objects "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"at build time"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and writes a\nplain stylesheet. Nothing about styling happens in the browser except applying\nclass names. Kirana is this kind, and it is exactly what the React team\nrecommends: static CSS files for static styles, and a custom property in\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"style","source":"style"}},{"type":"text","value":" for a value only known at runtime."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The complaint"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime CSS-in-JS"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styles are computed while rendering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No. Styles become CSS during the build"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A styling runtime in the bundle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, the whole library"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A module with only static styles imports nothing; merging and bridging need a helper under 1.1 kB gzipped"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server rendering collects styles"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No. The stylesheet is a file, linked like any other"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">style</span>&gt;","source":"<style>"}},{"type":"text","value":" tags inserted at runtime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never. The runtime "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/dynamic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"never generates CSS"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSS grows with markup"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Often, one rule per usage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/advanced/output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Atomic"}]},{"type":"text","value":": one rule per distinct declaration, shared by every element that uses it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Class names you cannot read"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hashed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hashed too, but "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> trace file:line property","source":"kirana-style trace file:line property"}},{"type":"text","value":" prints every entry for a style and the one that wins, and "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hovering it in the editor"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows the same"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Order bugs between style sheets"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Insertion order decided"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/precedence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"precedence ladder"}]},{"type":"text","value":", in "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/config/layers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"layers"}]}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you keep from CSS-in-JS is the part people liked: styles are values, next to\nthe component, typed, passed as props, and deleted with the component."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"you-can-see-the-css-again","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can see the CSS again"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime cost was one reason teams left CSS-in-JS. The other was reading. A\nTailwind class list "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"is"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the CSS, written on the element: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"grid gap-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span> p-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">md:</span>p-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">6</span>","source":"grid gap-4 p-4 md:p-6"}},{"type":"text","value":" tells you what the "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">article</span>&gt;","source":"<article>"}},{"type":"text","value":" gets without leaving the line. A style\nobject moves that into a constant somewhere else, and reading a component turns\ninto jumping to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">card</span>","source":"styles.card"}},{"type":"text","value":" and back."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana's "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"language server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" gives the class list back,\nwithout putting it in your markup:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At the end of every element's line"}]},{"type":"text","value":", what it ends up with, in a class list's\nwords and coloured by kind: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"▦ grid · gap 1rem · p 1rem · md: p <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span>.5rem","source":"▦ grid · gap 1rem · p 1rem · md: p 1.5rem"}},{"type":"text","value":". Values\nunder a guard lead with it ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"featured: shadow lg","source":"featured: shadow lg"}},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On hover"}]},{"type":"text","value":", a card: the box model drawn as DevTools draws it, every\ndeclaration with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"rem","source":"rem"}},{"type":"text","value":" in pixels and the token it reads, and the compiled rule.\nOn one property, every entry in precedence order and the step that decided."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In VS Code"}]},{"type":"text","value":", a Style Inspector that follows the cursor and turns "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"md","source":"md"}},{"type":"text","value":" on to show what applies then, and Style Fold, which reads a long object as\nits summary until you edit it, like Tailwind Fold, for objects."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It works in "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":".<span class=\"th-token th-property\">tsx</span>","source":".tsx"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":".<span class=\"th-token th-property\">vue</span>","source":".vue"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":".<span class=\"th-token th-property\">svelte</span>","source":".svelte"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":".<span class=\"th-token th-property\">astro</span>","source":".astro"}},{"type":"text","value":" files and Angular templates, in VS Code, Zed,\nNeovim and Helix. It answers from the compiler session the build uses, so the\neditor and the stylesheet never disagree."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So the trade is no longer readability for types. You keep what made object\nstyles worth it (a typo is a compile error, a token is a typed import, a style is\na value you pass and delete with its component), and the output is still atomic:\none rule per distinct declaration, shared by every element that uses it. On the\nsame three applications built three ways, Kirana 0.2.1's cold\nbuilds are level with Tailwind and 1.6× faster than StyleX (SWC), and its\nCSS and JavaScript, gzipped, are 2 % smaller than StyleX (SWC) and\n2 % smaller than Tailwind. Every measure, with its confidence interval, is on the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/project/benchmarks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"benchmarks page"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-stylex-got-right-and-what-kirana-adds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What StyleX got right, and what Kirana adds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"StyleX, which Meta open-sourced at the end of 2023, showed that compiled, atomic\nCSS-in-JS works at scale. Kirana keeps its premise: atomic output, constants\nthat cost nothing until used, styles as values passed through one prop, and\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">light-dark</span>()","source":"light-dark()"}},{"type":"text","value":" colours."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same shadcn/ui app, ported from Tailwind to StyleX (0.19) for comparison,\nshows these problems, each measured and written down with evidence. Kirana\nanswers them:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the StyleX port"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Kirana"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No descendant selectors: every "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[&amp;_svg]</span>","source":"[&_svg]"}},{"type":"text","value":" became a custom property handed down and read by the child"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/contextual","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"select.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">child</span>","source":"select.child"}},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"select.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">descendant</span>","source":"select.descendant"}}]},{"type":"text","value":", in a layer below the target's own styles, so the child's own size still wins"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A marker on the wrong element compiled and never matched, 36 times"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/relations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Relations"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are declared; a read without an anchor, or an anchor that cannot match, is a compile error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A shorthand lost to a longhand regardless of order ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"padding: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">0</span>","source":"padding: 0"}},{"type":"text","value":" did not beat "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"paddingTop","source":"paddingTop"}},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styles "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/merging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"merge per longhand"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"default: null","source":"default: null"}},{"type":"text","value":" removed a value where the author meant \"nothing here\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omitting keeps; "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"base: null","source":"base: null"}},{"type":"text","value":" removes, and only when you write it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@media","source":"@media"}},{"type":"text","value":" outranked "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":" and attributes, the reverse of Tailwind"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One ladder, stated and "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/debugging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"traceable"}]},{"type":"text","value":": state beats breakpoint, as in Tailwind"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom-property assignments were emitted unlayered and beat conditions beside them"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nothing is emitted outside a layer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens had to live in "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"*.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">stylex</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">ts</span>","source":"*.stylex.ts"}},{"type":"text","value":" files and be imported by name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens are ordinary exports, imported any way TypeScript allows"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" passed to a component that ignores it, or spread past a wrapper, was silent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx-on-external-component","source":"sx-on-external-component"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unused-sx","source":"unused-sx"}},{"type":"text","value":", including one module away"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Six silent bug classes needed a hand-written checking script; the lint plugin lagged the compiler and was turned off after ~150 false positives"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/diagnostics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"45 diagnostics"}]},{"type":"text","value":" come from the compiler itself; the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/lint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lint plugin"}]},{"type":"text","value":" reads the compiler's own validation instead of re-implementing it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The official compiler is Babel; the Rust one is a community port behind it"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine is Kirana's own, in Rust on "},{"type":"link","href":"https://oxc.rs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"oxc"}]},{"type":"text","value":", with a WASI build that writes the same bytes where no native one runs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No utility vocabulary: a Tailwind team rebuilt the scales by hand"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tokens/preset-scales","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@kirana-style/preset-scales","source":"@kirana-style/preset-scales"}}]},{"type":"text","value":" is Tailwind v4's scales, and "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/utilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"utility strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" compile to the same atoms as the object form"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A port from Tailwind was done by hand"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-tailwind","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> migrate tailwind","source":"kirana-style migrate tailwind"}}]},{"type":"text","value":", measured below"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework reach is the other half: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" works in React, Preact, Solid, Qwik, Vue, Svelte, Astro, Angular and Ember (Angular\ntemplates take it as a directive, Ember's as a helper), and Kirana has adapters\nfor Vite, Rolldown, webpack, Rspack, Rsbuild, Parcel, Bun and esbuild, with Next.js on Turbopack or webpack. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"frameworks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"StyleX has things Kirana does not: it is published, used in production at Meta\nand elsewhere, and has a community. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-stylex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from StyleX"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nis honest about that."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-not-tailwind-and-cn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why not Tailwind and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cn()"},{"type":"text","value":"?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tailwind is excellent, and Kirana borrows its vocabulary on purpose. What Kirana\nreplaces is the merging. A component library built on Tailwind lets callers\noverride styles by appending classes, and resolves conflicts at runtime with\ntailwind-merge ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">cn</span>()","source":"cn()"}},{"type":"text","value":"), which parses class strings in the browser and keeps the\nlast class of each conflict group. Measured with tailwind-merge 3.6.0:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What happened"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">twMerge</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;px-2 py-1&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;p-3&quot;</span>)","source":"twMerge(\"px-2 py-1\", \"p-3\")"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"p-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">3</span>","source":"p-3"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Correct: the later padding replaces both axes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">twMerge</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;text-sm&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;text-[0.8rem]&quot;</span>)","source":"twMerge(\"text-sm\", \"text-[0.8rem]\")"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[0.8rem]</span>","source":"text-[0.8rem]"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-sm","source":"text-sm"}},{"type":"text","value":" is deleted whole, so its paired "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"line height"}]},{"type":"text","value":" goes too, and the element now inherits one"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">twMerge</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;shadow-sm&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;shadow-glow&quot;</span>)","source":"twMerge(\"shadow-sm\", \"shadow-glow\")"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"shadow-sm shadow-glow","source":"shadow-sm shadow-glow"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A custom value it was not told about is not a conflict; CSS source order decides which shadow shows"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">twMerge</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;text-sm&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;text-brand&quot;</span>)","source":"twMerge(\"text-sm\", \"text-brand\")"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-sm text-brand","source":"text-sm text-brand"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It cannot know whether "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-brand","source":"text-brand"}},{"type":"text","value":" is a size or a colour without configuration ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"extendTailwindMerge","source":"extendTailwindMerge"}},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None of these is a bug in tailwind-merge; it works from class names, because\nclass names are all it has. Kirana merges "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"declarations"}]},{"type":"text","value":", at build time, per\nlonghand: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"fontSize","source":"fontSize"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"lineHeight","source":"lineHeight"}},{"type":"text","value":" are separate entries, a custom token is a\ntyped value, and there is nothing to configure or parse at runtime. And a typo\n("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-smm","source":"text-smm"}},{"type":"text","value":") is a compile error, not a class that silently does nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"it-doubles-the-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"It doubles the code\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is the most common first reaction, and it is true in one sense: a style object\ntakes more "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lines"}]},{"type":"text","value":" than a class string. It does not contain more "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"meaning"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"// Tailwind: one line, read left to right\n<button className=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-accent disabled:opacity-50\" />\n\n// Kirana: the same declarations, one per line\nconst button = css({\n  display: \"inline-flex\",\n  alignItems: \"center\",\n  gap: space[2],\n  borderRadius: radius.md,\n  paddingInline: space[4],\n  paddingBlock: space[2],\n  fontSize: fontSize.sm,\n  lineHeight: lineHeight.sm,\n  fontWeight: fontWeight.medium,\n  backgroundColor: { \":hover\": theme.accent },\n  opacity: { \":disabled\": 0.5 },\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Tailwind: one line, read left to right</span>\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">button</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">className</span>=<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-accent disabled:opacity-50&quot;</span> /&gt;\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Kirana: the same declarations, one per line</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> button = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">display</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;inline-flex&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">alignItems</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;center&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">gap</span>: space[<span class=\"th-token th-number\">2</span>],\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">borderRadius</span>: radius.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">md</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingInline</span>: space[<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span>],\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingBlock</span>: space[<span class=\"th-token th-number\">2</span>],\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">fontSize</span>: fontSize.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">sm</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">lineHeight</span>: lineHeight.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">sm</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">fontWeight</span>: fontWeight.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">medium</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">backgroundColor</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:hover&quot;</span>: theme.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">accent</span> },\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">opacity</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:disabled&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">0.5</span> },\n})"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tailwind is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"horizontal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"; Kirana is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"vertical"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The vertical form earns its\nlines:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diffs and reviews show one change per line."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Changing the padding changes\none line, not a 120-character string where the reviewer hunts for "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"px-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span>","source":"px-4"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conditions group by property."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Everything that can happen to the background\ncolour is in one place; in a class string, its "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"bg-","source":"bg-"}},{"type":"text","value":" utilities and their\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">hover:</span>","source":"hover:"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">dark:</span>","source":"dark:"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">data-[state=open]:</span>","source":"data-[state=open]:"}},{"type":"text","value":" forms can sit anywhere in the line."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nothing is implicit."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"text-sm","source":"text-sm"}},{"type":"text","value":" sets two properties; the object says so.\nThe single most common drift in our port was a font size without its line\nheight."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every key and value is typed."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Autocompletion, go-to-definition on tokens,\nrename, and errors before the build."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styles have names."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">header</span>","source":"styles.header"}},{"type":"text","value":" says what it is for; the markup stays\nreadable because the styling is not inline in it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comments fit."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A line can say why a value is what it is."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And you do not have to choose one form for a whole project. With the scales\npreset, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>=<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;px-4 py-2 text-sm&quot;</span>","source":"sx=\"px-4 py-2 text-sm\""}},{"type":"text","value":" is valid Kirana and compiles to the same atoms as\nthe object. Use strings where a short line reads best and objects where a\ncomponent has states. The compiler also does not care how long your source is:\nthe output is atomic either way, and a declaration used in a hundred components\nis still one rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-kirana-costs-you-something","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where Kirana costs you something"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is before 1.0."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A minor version may still change the API, and its\nrelease notes say how to move; see "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/project/status","children":[{"type":"text","value":"what works today"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is a compiler."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Styles must be statically known in shape: a computed key\nor a spread object is an error, and a value the compiler cannot enumerate goes\nthrough a custom property."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is stricter than CSS."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Contextual rules rank below the target's own\nstyles, and two conditions that tie are reported instead of left to source\norder. That is what makes the result predictable, and it is why a migration\nfrom Tailwind needs a few hand fixes (the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-tailwind","children":[{"type":"text","value":"migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nlists every one we met)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The richest editor is VS Code."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Every LSP editor gets the card, the hints\nand the fixes; the Style Inspector, Style Fold and coloured hints are VS\nCode's. The VS Code extension is on the Marketplace and Open VSX; Zed's\ninstalls as a dev extension until it is in Zed's registry."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"why-kirana","text":"Why Kirana","level":1},{"id":"the-css-in-js-people-left","text":"The CSS-in-JS people left","level":2},{"id":"what-a-compiler-changes","text":"What a compiler changes","level":2},{"id":"you-can-see-the-css-again","text":"You can see the CSS again","level":2},{"id":"what-stylex-got-right-and-what-kirana-adds","text":"What StyleX got right, and what Kirana adds","level":2},{"id":"why-not-tailwind-and-cn","text":"Why not Tailwind and cn()?","level":2},{"id":"it-doubles-the-code","text":"\"It doubles the code\"","level":2},{"id":"where-kirana-costs-you-something","text":"Where Kirana costs you something","level":2}]}
